{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal at all. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides the cleanest possible comparison to the existing baseline: same profile setting (singleprofile), same simplicity level (no aggregation, no fusion), differing only in modality. If image_only approaches or exceeds 0.485, it confirms image features are informative and justifies investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion. If it falls well below, it suggests RNA is the primary signal source, allowing us to prune all multimodal configs and focus budget on RNA encoder/aggregation choices. This single experiment resolves the largest structural design question (modality value) while keeping the comparison maximally controlled, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

